---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SpecTable from '../components/SpecTable.astro';
import CartridgeCard from '../components/CartridgeCard.astro';
import FaqSchema from '../components/FaqSchema.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Indiana Deer Season Dates 2026-27"
  description="Indiana's 2026-27 deer season dates, license costs, and rifle rules — archery, youth, firearms, and muzzleloader season, all in one place, updated yearly."
>
  <section class="pillar">
    <div class="wrap pillar__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Season Dates — Indiana</p>
      <h1>Indiana Deer Season Dates: 2026-27</h1>
      <p class="pillar__intro">
        Indiana's 2026-27 deer firearms season runs Nov. 14–29, 2026. Archery runs Oct. 1, 2026–Jan. 3, 2027 and muzzleloader runs Dec. 5–20. The statewide bag limit is one antlered and six antlerless deer, combined. This isn't a dated field note; we refresh it in
        place each year when the DNR publishes new dates.
      </p>
      <p class="pillar__updated">Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>

      <h2>2026-27 Indiana Deer Season Dates at a Glance</h2>

      <SpecTable
        caption="Indiana Deer Season Dates — 2026-27"
        compareColumns={["2026-27"]}
        metricRows={[
          { label: "Youth Season", values: ["Sept. 26–27, 2026"] },
          { label: "Archery", values: ["Oct. 1, 2026 – Jan. 3, 2027"] },
          { label: "Firearms", values: ["Nov. 14–29, 2026"] },
          { label: "Muzzleloader", values: ["Dec. 5–20, 2026"] },
          { label: "Bag Limit", values: ["1 antlered + 6 antlerless, combined"] },
        ]}
        note="Source: Indiana DNR's 2026-27 Hunting & Trapping Guide and deer hunting seasons page. Deer Reduction Zones run separately, Sept. 15, 2026 – Jan. 31, 2027, with a 10-deer limit and earn-a-buck requirement."
      />

      <h2>Indiana's Statewide Bag Limit: 1 Buck, 6 Antlerless</h2>
      <p>
        Indiana's bag limit is the most clear-cut of the seven states in this region: <strong>one
        antlered deer and six antlerless deer, combined, across youth, archery, firearms, and
        muzzleloader seasons.</strong> County antlerless quotas can cap you below the statewide
        six, so check your county before you plan a multi-deer season. Deer Reduction Zones run
        on their own separate calendar (Sept. 15, 2026 – Jan. 31, 2027) with a 10-deer limit and
        an earn-a-buck requirement.
      </p>

      <h2>Can You Hunt With a Straight-Wall Cartridge in Indiana?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes — but it isn't required anymore. Indiana dropped its straight-wall case-shape
        requirement, one of three states in this region to do so in the last two seasons.
      </p>
      <CartridgeCard
        name="Indiana"
        url="https://www.in.gov/dnr/fish-and-wildlife/hunting-and-trapping/hunting-trapping-guide/deer-hunting-questions-and-answers/"
        linkRel="noopener"
        description="No shape requirement as of the 2025–26 season. Any centerfire rifle cartridge, public or private land. 10-round possession limit for such cartridges."
        stats={[
          { label: "Case Shape", value: "Not required (2025–26)" },
          { label: "Min Diameter", value: ".219in (5.56mm)+" },
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        Want to see how your cartridge actually flies? Try our <a href="/ballistics-comparison/">ballistics comparison tool</a> or read <a href="/blog/straight-wall-vs-shouldered-ballistics-comparison/">Straight-Wall vs Shouldered Ballistics</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Running a breech-loaded muzzleloader like a FireStick or NitroFire during muzzleloader
        season instead? It's legal this season via a fast-tracked interim rule, with the
        permanent version still working through Indiana's Natural Resources Commission — see our <a href="/blog/firestick-nitrofire-muzzleloader-legality-2026/">FireStick &amp; NitroFire legality guide</a> for
        the latest on where that vote stands, and our <a href="/blog/straight-wall-cartridge-state-regulations/">straight-wall cartridge regulations guide</a> for
        how Indiana compares to the other six states in this region.
      </p>

      <h2>Indiana Deer License Costs, 2026-27</h2>
      <p>
        A resident annual hunting license is $20. Single-season deer licenses (archery, firearm,
        or muzzleloader) run $39 each, or you can buy the Deer License Bundle for $91, which
        covers two antlerless tags and one antlered tag across every season.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nonresidents pay $90 for the hunting license and $240 per single-season deer license, or
        $550 for the full bundle. Everything is over the counter — no draw, no application
        window. Indiana's license year runs April 1 through March 31, and hunter education is
        required for anyone born after Dec. 31, 1986.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the full seven-state cost and lottery breakdown — including how Indiana stacks up
        against Ohio, Michigan, Iowa, Illinois, Minnesota, and Wisconsin — see our <a href="/blog/deer-hunting-license-guide-seven-state/">Deer Hunting License Guide: 7-State Corn Belt Edition</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Plan Your Whole Indiana Season</h2>
      <p>
        A few more things worth lining up against the dates above before opening day:
      </p>
      <ul class="pillar__crosslinks">
        <li><a href="/blog/indiana-double-crop-wheat-soybean-calendar/">Indiana's Double-Crop Wheat-Soybean Calendar and Early-October Bedding Shifts</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/firestick-nitrofire-muzzleloader-legality-2026/">FireStick &amp; NitroFire Muzzleloaders: Legal States 2026-27</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/2026-deer-season-regulations-seven-state-roundup/">2026 Deer Season Regulations: 7-State Bag Limits Guide</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>More Corn Belt Season-Date Guides</h2>
      <ul class="pillar__crosslinks pillar__hub">
        <li><a href="/ohio-deer-season-dates/">Ohio Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/michigan-deer-season-dates/">Michigan Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/iowa-deer-season-dates/">Iowa Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/illinois-deer-season-dates/">Illinois Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/minnesota-deer-season-dates/">Minnesota Deer Season Dates</a></li>
        <li><a href="/wisconsin-deer-season-dates/">Wisconsin Deer Season Dates</a></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="pillar__cta">
        <picture class="pillar__cta-cover">
          <source srcset="/images/perfect-window-cover.webp" type="image/webp" />
          <img src="/images/perfect-window-cover.jpg" alt="The Perfect Window book cover" width="500" height="647" loading="lazy" />
        </picture>
        <div class="pillar__cta-body">
          <p class="pillar__cta-title">Want every state's dates in one place?</p>
          <p class="pillar__cta-desc">
            <em>The Perfect Window</em> lays out harvest timing, rut windows, and legal season
            dates across all 12 Corn Belt states on one visual overlap chart — handy if you hunt
            more than just Indiana.
          </p>
          <a class="pillar__cta-link" href="https://link.amazon/B03KhoZDf" rel="sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Get it on Amazon &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>FAQ</h2>

      <p><strong>Is Indiana a straight-wall cartridge state?</strong><br />
      Not anymore. Indiana dropped its straight-wall case-shape requirement as of the 2025–26
      season — any centerfire rifle cartridge with a bullet diameter of .219" (5.56mm) or
      larger is legal now, on public or private land.</p>

      <p><strong>When does Indiana's 2026-27 deer archery season start?</strong><br />
      Thursday, Oct. 1, 2026, running through Sunday, Jan. 3, 2027.</p>

      <p><strong>What's Indiana's deer bag limit?</strong><br />
      One antlered deer and six antlerless deer, combined, across youth, archery, firearms, and
      muzzleloader seasons — county quotas can cap the antlerless number lower.</p>

      <p><strong>How much does an Indiana deer license cost?</strong><br />
      A resident hunting license is $20, plus $39 per single-season deer license (or $91 for the
      full bundle). Nonresidents pay $90 for the license and $240 per deer license, or $550 for
      the bundle.</p>

      <FaqSchema items={[
        { question: "Is Indiana a straight-wall cartridge state?", answer: "Not anymore. Indiana dropped its straight-wall case-shape requirement as of the 2025-26 season - any centerfire rifle cartridge with a bullet diameter of .219in (5.56mm) or larger is legal now, on public or private land." },
        { question: "When does Indiana's 2026-27 deer archery season start?", answer: "Thursday, Oct. 1, 2026, running through Sunday, Jan. 3, 2027." },
        { question: "What's Indiana's deer bag limit?", answer: "One antlered deer and six antlerless deer, combined, across youth, archery, firearms, and muzzleloader seasons - county quotas can cap the antlerless number lower." },
        { question: "How much does an Indiana deer license cost?", answer: "A resident hunting license is $20, plus $39 per single-season deer license, or $91 for the full bundle. Nonresidents pay $90 for the license and $240 per deer license, or $550 for the bundle." }
      ]} />
      <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "WebPage",
        name: "Indiana Deer Season Dates 2026-27",
        url: "https://cornfedbucks.com/indiana-deer-season-dates/",
        dateModified: "2026-10-01",
        inLanguage: "en-US",
        isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "CornfedBucks", url: "https://cornfedbucks.com/" },
        author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Nick" }
      })} />

      <p class="pillar__disclaimer">
        Season dates and bag limits sourced from Indiana DNR's 2026-27 Hunting &amp; Trapping
        Guide and deer hunting seasons page. County- or zone-level exceptions can override
        anything listed here — always confirm current rules at <a href="https://www.in.gov/dnr/fish-and-wildlife/hunting-and-trapping/deer-hunting/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">in.gov/dnr</a> before
        you buy a license or head afield.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .pillar { padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .pillar__inner { max-width: 720px; }
  .pillar h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .pillar__intro {
    color: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0.85;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
  }
  .pillar .pillar__updated {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--stalk);
    margin: -1.1rem 0 1.75rem;
  }
  .pillar h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.6rem);
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .pillar p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .pillar__crosslinks {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .pillar__cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--husk);
    border: 1px solid var(--stalk);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 2.25rem;
  }
  .pillar__cta-cover { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 84px; }
  .pillar__cta-cover img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 3px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(34, 27, 20, 0.25);
  }
  .pillar__cta-body { min-width: 0; }
  .pillar__cta-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }
  .pillar__cta-desc { font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .pillar__cta-link {
    font-family: var(--font-tag);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--blaze);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .pillar__cta-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .pillar__cta { flex-direction: column; }
    .pillar__cta-cover { width: 100px; }
  }

  .pillar__disclaimer {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--stalk);
    line-height: 1.6;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--husk);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
